The first is "this apple is sweet".
The second is "this apple is sour".
The firstwords is split first by " ".
The secondwords is split second by " ".
Keep a shared vocabulary as an empty list of text.
Keep a shared counts as an empty list of whole numbers.
Keep a shared sought as empty text.
Keep a shared foundat as 0.
To find from spot (a whole number).
If spot is more than the last position of vocabulary, set foundat to -1, return.
If item spot of vocabulary matches sought, set foundat to spot, return.
Find from spot plus 1.

To record.
Set foundat to -1.
Find from 0.
The local is foundat.
If local is at least 0, set item local of counts to item local of counts plus 1, return.
The fresh is a copy of sought.
Place fresh into vocabulary.
Place 1 into counts.

For each piece in firstwords.
Set sought to piece.
Record.

For each piece in secondwords.
Set sought to piece.
Record.

For every spot from 0 to the last position of vocabulary.
If item spot of counts is 1, show item spot of vocabulary.
